{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1083940-magic-and-outer-space","id":1083940,"title":"Magic and Outer Space.","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-04-26T06:37:00-07:00","id":1083940,"title":"Magic and Outer Space.","content":"I have heard that magic doesn't work in outer space(With the usual exception of archmastery), but I cannot find anything that would indicate that this is the case other than a quote from unofficial errata.<br /> <br /> Is it impossible for mages to work magic in space? If so, why?<br /> <br /> Or is magic just different in space? Is it the same?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9312-myradmir","name":"Myradmir","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"110"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-26T06:44:00-07:00","id":1083941,"title":"","content":"I can't think why it wouldn't...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2291-gwyn-chan-r-gwyll","name":"Gwyn chan 'r Gwyll","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-26T06:46:41-07:00","id":1083942,"title":"","content":"In second edition there's nothing (except from purely practical reasons) that stops a mage from working their magic in space. I'm not familiar enough with first edition to say. But I do recall hearing that in Mage: The Ascension there was some kind of limit to magic in space.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-26T07:33:59-07:00","id":1083964,"title":"","content":"I think Old Mages issues with Magic in Space were mostly to do with how Magick was linked to things like Paradigm and Consensual Reality, issues that arent overly relevant to NMage. I don't see any particular issues with spell casting in space, aside from it being somewhat impractical of course. Also it might be a tad dull, unless your ST is planning to throw some X-Files stuff into your Occult Horror game?<br /> <br /> If you have a PC who wants to visit other planets, I might recommend taking a plunge into the Astral Seas and touring their reflections in the Temenos. Adventure AND Enlightnenment await! Watch out for the Martian Death Rays","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6230-katana1515","name":"Katana1515","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6230_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"280"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-26T08:11:10-07:00","id":1083979,"title":"","content":"I believe it comes from the original FAQ by Bill Bridges. I don't know why exactly, though it may have been a carry over from Ars Magica.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-27T06:32:38-07:00","id":1084452,"title":"","content":"There's no reason it wouldn't work in 2nd edition. In fact, I've had to (jokingly) house rule in my game that just because you can see the Moon, it doesn't mean that it's in sensory range.<br /> <br /> Most of the problem with mages and doing crazy things like teleporting to the moon or another planet revolve around how difficult it is to get there and then survive there. Can't teleport to the moon because you don't have any sympathetic connection to the moon. Same for another planet. Where could you find such things? I'd say out in the astral solar system of the Anima Mundi. A mage who wants to go to Mars can start his adventure by going inwards into the Astral and then finding a sympathetic connection lingering on Sidereal Mars.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13082-projectmoon","name":"projectmoon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-27T06:43:30-07:00","id":1084456,"title":"","content":"The astral does not have sympathetic connections with the things they represent. Spatial sympathy comes from direct interaction. The best bet to find a sympathetic connection to the Moon or Mars is finding a sample brought back to Earth.<br /> <br /> Also, you don't have to house rule the moon being out of sensory range since it's impossible to target something of that Size anyway, and the naked eye can't distinguish areas small enough for AoE spells.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-27T06:49:07-07:00","id":1084460,"title":"","content":"I mean, reasonably, you can't teleport to the moon because you will suffocate and die. NASA filmed fake moon landings after the real ones just found huge piles of dead warlocks everywhere.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12109-urbenmyth","name":"Urbenmyth","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"166"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-27T06:53:17-07:00","id":1084462,"title":"","content":"Well, if you used Space to get to the moon you'd reasonably use Co-Location, and since you don't suffocate under a single turn you could just hop right back home.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-27T07:08:57-07:00","id":1084466,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1083940-magic-and-outer-space?p=1084456#post1084456\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The astral does not have sympathetic connections with the things they represent. Spatial sympathy comes from direct interaction. The best bet to find a sympathetic connection to the Moon or Mars is finding a sample brought back to Earth.<br /> <br /> Also, you don't have to house rule the moon being out of sensory range since it's impossible to target something of that Size anyway, and the naked eye can't distinguish areas small enough for AoE spells.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's more about what you'd find in the Astral that might have sympathetic connections to the planetary body. The Anima Mundi is very specifically full of all sorts of strange stuff, so who knows what's out there? It would definitely not be something like &quot;Make 3 dice rolls to get into the Anima Mundi, then an Investigation roll to find your connection.&quot; It would be a good basis for a story.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I mean, reasonably, you can't teleport to the moon because you will suffocate and die. NASA filmed fake moon landings after the real ones just found huge piles of dead warlocks everywhere. </div> </div> </div>I'd assume that any mage with plans to go into outer space is probably going to protect themselves against the effects some way or another (mundane or magically).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13082-projectmoon","name":"projectmoon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-27T07:16:16-07:00","id":1084470,"title":"","content":"If you used Zoom In you could probably get visual, up to date information in enough granular detail to be able to teleport to the moon via Remote Viewing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-27T09:19:28-07:00","id":1084514,"title":"","content":"You could just rule that light older than 1 second no longer qualifies as sensory. That would prevent lunar teleports, since the &quot;moon&quot; you are seeing is just reflected light that has gone too stale. For most terrestrial distances, you'd never encounter that limit to be able to tell it is there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-27T09:23:10-07:00","id":1084516,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1083940-magic-and-outer-space?p=1084514#post1084514\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You could just rule that light older than 1 second no longer qualifies as sensory. That would prevent lunar teleports, since the &quot;moon&quot; you are seeing is just reflected light that has gone too stale. For most terrestrial distances, you'd never encounter that limit to be able to tell it is there.</div> </div> </div> </div>Time Compelling will be enough to nullify the difference on short distances.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-27T10:27:17-07:00","id":1084545,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1083940-magic-and-outer-space?p=1084456#post1084456\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The astral does not have sympathetic connections with the things they represent. Spatial sympathy comes from direct interaction. The best bet to find a sympathetic connection to the Moon or Mars is finding a sample brought back to Earth.<br /> <br /> Also, you don't have to house rule the moon being out of sensory range since it's impossible to target something of that Size anyway, and the naked eye can't distinguish areas small enough for AoE spells.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually, I seem to recall it being mentioned, I think only in implication by Dave in some post or another, that the true astral representation of other planets <i>would</i> have Sympathy with the real thing. And by true representation I mean those in the sidereal wastes, not simply peoples ideas of what something is that you'd find in the Temenos.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-27T10:48:15-07:00","id":1084570,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ashenrogue</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1083940-magic-and-outer-space?p=1084545#post1084545\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Actually, I seem to recall it being mentioned, I think only in implication by Dave in some post or another, that the true astral representation of other planets <i>would</i> have Sympathy with the real thing. And by true representation I mean those in the sidereal wastes, not simply peoples ideas of what something is that you'd find in the Temenos.</div> </div> </div> </div>Making that kind of trip is an epic enough journey that I would allow it based on rule of cool alone.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6230-katana1515","name":"Katana1515","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6230_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"280"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-27T11:08:52-07:00","id":1084584,"title":"","content":"You could use forces to fly to the moon in a ship or something maybe a submarine.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-27T11:23:50-07:00","id":1084592,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Katana1515</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1083940-magic-and-outer-space?p=1084570#post1084570\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Making that kind of trip is an epic enough journey that I would allow it based on rule of cool alone.</div> </div> </div> </div>Pretty much. If you care enough about it to dive that deep into the Astral then you obviously care enough that you want to make a story out of it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}